// Inventory (plan A1 §2.1 "Quantities", "Append-only", §2.4 D, §2.5 "Lot"; PLAN §1.3, §2.8 "Cr VI", §4.7 stages
// 09a-receive, 09b-cr6, 11a-issue and the end check "the stock ledger reconciles"; features SCM-113, SCM-116, SCM-117,
// SCM-176, SCM-184, SCM-187, SCM-189, SCM-194, SCM-232, SCM-233, SCM-247, SCM-253, QHS-029): the locations of each site,
// goods receipts against purchase orders, lots (a dye batch, a roll batch, a protector batch) with their quality hold
// and Cr VI result, hides one by one, the append-only stock ledger and its valuation. apps/factory-api's modules write
// them (B-W1-22 locations and ledger, B-W1-32 receipts in the office, B-W1-33 on the floor, B-W1-34 the Cr VI release,
// B-W1-35 opening stock, B-W1-39 issue to the work order), always through command().
//
// The stock ledger (StockMove, `@append-only`) is the truth: every movement is one row (a receipt, an issue to a work
// order, a return from it, a transfer, an adjustment, a count difference, a scrap, the opening stock) with its item,
// colour, lot and hide, its quantity as entered and in the item's base unit, the location it leaves and the one it
// enters (none: outside the site's stock: the supplier, the work order, the bin), its document and who and which
// device posted it, when. Quantities are always above 0: the locations give the direction. A mistake is fixed by a new
// row: a reversal (the same move with its locations swapped, at most one per move) or an adjustment with its reason.
//
// Balances are DERIVED, not stored: on hand at a location = the sum of the moves into it − the sum of the moves out of
// it, per site, item, colour, lot and hide. So the ledger reconciles by construction (no projection to rebuild). The
// …_supply_guards trigger refuses a move that would take a location below zero (SCM-194: no double use), under a
// transaction lock per location and stock key, and refuses to ISSUE a lot that is not RELEASED. A receipt is POSTED
// only when the ledger holds exactly its lines' quantities (checked at commit).
//
// Quality (A1 §2.5, SCM-117, QHS-029): a lot is QUARANTINE → RELEASED, or REJECTED or BLOCKED; a hide follows its lot.
// A lot of leather that needs the Cr VI test (REACH Annex XVII entry 47: below 3 mg/kg) is RELEASED only with its Cr VI
// result PASS (what counts as evidence is a setting, Q14: a report per lot, or a supplier report covering the article
// and period). Only RELEASED stock is usable: planning nets only it, and only it is issued.
//
// Valuation (A1 §2.6: costs never reach the floor or a partner): StockValuation, `@append-only`, office only, holds the
// cost of each move that changes the site's stock value (a transfer inside the site changes none): signed base quantity,
// unit cost and amount. It is a ledger of its own, not columns of the move, because the floor posts moves: its column
// grants would leave a cost column out of its insert, and the move could never be valued afterwards (append-only). The
// office values its own moves in the same command; a system handler values the floor's moves after their event.
//
// Who sees what (ownership/inventory.json): the office reads and writes; the floor reads and writes the stock of its
// own site (receives goods and hides, posts moves, changes a hide's state; never releases a lot, never sees a value);
// portal and link sessions read nothing here. Nobody deletes a location, lot, hide or receipt (archived, rejected,
// scrapped, cancelled or reversed instead); the office deletes only the lines of an OPEN receipt.
//
// Units (A1 §2.1, SCM-184, SCM-187): Decimal(18,4) with an explicit unit (enum Uom), never a float; each hide carries
// its own measured area, and stock is the sum of the hides, never a count times an average. Physical rows carry their
// site (and company), and every reference between them includes it, so a row can never point at another site's row.
//
// W2b (schema wave 1/7, B-W2b-01; the B-W2a-11, -31, -43, -44 and -48 notes): a move keeps the reason code it was made
// for (write-off, adjustment, production scrap) as data instead of a note prefix; goods back from a customer, goods back
// to a supplier and garments leaving with a shipment have reasons of their own (CUSTOMER_RETURN naming its return line,
// SUPPLIER_RETURN, SHIPMENT naming its shipment line) instead of an ADJUSTMENT; a hide sent back to the tannery is
// RETURNED; a SCRAPPED or RETURNED hide comes back to the state it had (previousState, kept by the database) once the move
// that took it out is reversed; a posted receipt's supplier DDT number and date can be corrected, with when, who and why
// (the …_followups_stock_w2b_guards triggers).
//
// W2b (schema wave 12/16, B-W2b-80; leather.prisma): a hide names its leather grade and shade group as records too
// (Hide.gradeId, shadeGroupId; the texts stay, and say the same); an offcut worth keeping comes back with a move of its own
// (REMNANT, RETURN's twin) and is a tagged Remnant.
//
// W2b-5 (schema wave 36/44, B-W2b-277; warehouse-depth.prisma): locations of more kinds (a customer's, in transit, a pick
// face, bulk), blocked with a reason and labelled with the code a scan confirms; goods without a purchase order wait in a
// holding place for a buyer; a lot has a lifecycle beside its quality status, a parent lot it was split from and its own
// attributes; a move has a posting date apart from the day it happened, and the transfer line it carries (TRANSFER_OUT and
// TRANSFER_IN between two sites: stock in transit stays on the from-site's TRANSIT location until it is received).
//
// W2b-5 (schema wave 39/44, B-W2b-281; SAL-306; sales-orders-depth.prisma): a customer's own material (leather, trims the
// brand sends for its orders) is stock the customer owns: its lots name their owner (Lot.ownerPartyId); it is never valued,
// never bought and never used for another party's order (the …_sales_orders_depth_w2b_guards triggers).

/// A place on a site where stock lies (SCM-176): a warehouse, a zone, a bin, the goods-in dock, the quarantine shelf,
/// a line-side supply point. A tree inside the site. Archived (never deleted) once used; an archived location takes no
/// more stock, and a location is archived only once it is empty.
model Location {
  id          String       @id @db.Uuid
  tenantId    String       @default(dbgenerated("(NULLIF(current_setting('factory.tenant_id'::text, true), ''::text))::uuid")) @db.Uuid
  companyId   String       @db.Uuid
  siteId      String       @db.Uuid
  /// The location it is inside (a bin in a zone, a zone in a warehouse), on the same site; null at the top.
  parentId    String?      @db.Uuid
  /// Short code, unique on the site; printed on the bin label and scanned.
  code        String
  name        String
  kind        LocationKind
  /// W2a (SCM-141): the workshop that holds it, exactly for a SUBCONTRACTOR location (a party with the SUBCONTRACTOR
  /// role); set when it is made and never changed (the …_supply_w2a_guards trigger). Its stock stays the company's.
  partyId     String?      @db.Uuid
  status      MasterStatus @default(ACTIVE)
  /// W2b-5 (schema wave 36/44, B-W2b-277; SCM-178): the code its bin label carries and a scan confirms (a put-away, a move,
  /// a count): unique in the tenant, so a scan names one place; 1 to 64 characters without spaces. null: no label yet.
  labelCode   String?
  /// W2b-5 (SCM-181): blocked: when, by whom, why (COUNT, DAMAGE, CLEAN_UP; OTHER says it in blockNote) and until which day
  /// (Europe/Rome; null: until it is unblocked, which clears all five). While blocked it takes no move in or out but a
  /// count's own COUNT moves (the …_warehouse_depth_w2b_guards trigger); a count blocks its locations while it runs.
  blockedAt   DateTime?            @db.Timestamptz(3)
  blockedById String?              @db.Uuid
  blockReason LocationBlockReason?
  blockNote   String?
  blockedUntil DateTime?           @db.Date
  version     Int          @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime     @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt   DateTime     @default(now()) @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  createdById String?      @db.Uuid

  site     Site        @relation(fields: [tenantId, companyId, siteId], references: [tenantId, companyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  // Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default for an optional relation: that would also clear tenantId and siteId.
  parent   Location?   @relation("LocationTree", fields: [tenantId, siteId, parentId], references: [tenantId, siteId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  children Location[]  @relation("LocationTree")
  // W2a stockcount.prisma: the counts under it, and the count lines of it.
  stockCounts     StockCount[]
  stockCountLines StockCountLine[]
  movesOut StockMove[] @relation("StockMoveFrom")
  movesIn  StockMove[] @relation("StockMoveTo")
  // W2a holds.prisma: the holds whose goods were moved here (a QUARANTINE place).
  qualityHolds QualityHold[]
  // W2a: the workshop of a SUBCONTRACTOR location, and the subcontract orders sent to it (subcontract.prisma).
  // Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default for an optional relation: that would also clear tenantId.
  party             Party?             @relation(fields: [tenantId, partyId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  subcontractOrders SubcontractOrder[]
  // W2b-5 supply.prisma (wave 40/44): the purchase orders delivered straight to it (a workshop's place).
  shipToPurchaseOrders PurchaseOrder[] @relation("PurchaseOrderShipToLocation")
  // W2b kits.prisma: the work-order kits staged here.
  workOrderKits     WorkOrderKit[]
  // W2b leather.prisma (wave 12/16): the remnants and fabric rolls lying here.
  remnants          Remnant[]
  fabricRolls       FabricRoll[]
  // W2b-5 warehouse-depth.prisma (wave 36/44): the defaults that name it; the transfers picked from, put into and in transit
  // on it, and their lines; the count schedules of it; the tasks from or to it; the goods without a PO held in it.
  defaultFor         DefaultLocation[]
  transfersFrom      TransferOrder[]   @relation("TransferOrderFrom")
  transfersTo        TransferOrder[]   @relation("TransferOrderTo")
  transfersInTransit TransferOrder[]   @relation("TransferOrderTransit")
  transferLinesFrom  TransferLine[]    @relation("TransferLineFrom")
  transferLinesTo    TransferLine[]    @relation("TransferLineTo")
  countSchedules     CountSchedule[]
  tasksFrom          WarehouseTask[]   @relation("WarehouseTaskFrom")
  tasksTo            WarehouseTask[]   @relation("WarehouseTaskTo")
  heldReceipts       GoodsReceipt[]    @relation("GoodsReceiptHolding")

  @@unique([tenantId, siteId, code])
  // The target of the tenant- and site-safe references from the moves and the child locations.
  @@unique([tenantId, siteId, id])
  // W2b-5: a bin label's code names one place in the tenant.
  @@unique([tenantId, labelCode])
}

enum LocationKind {
  WAREHOUSE
  ZONE
  BIN
  /// The goods-in dock.
  RECEIVING
  /// The quality-hold shelf (a lot's status is what holds it; the place only helps to find it).
  QUARANTINE
  /// A line-side supply point (the cutting room's leather rack).
  PRODUCTION
  SHIPPING
  /// W2a (SCM-141): our stock at an outside workshop (a terzista), owned by its party (Location.partyId).
  SUBCONTRACTOR
  /// W2a (GAP-003): finished garments ready to ship; a production receipt puts them here (or in a location inside one).
  FINISHED_GOODS
  /// W2b-5 (SCM-177): our stock at a customer's (consignment, a fitting stock), owned by its party (Location.partyId, a
  /// customer or brand).
  CUSTOMER
  /// W2b-5 (SCM-177, SCM-220): goods between two sites: a transfer's goods lie here, the from-site's stock, from the ship to
  /// the receipt; only a transfer's moves enter or leave it.
  TRANSIT
  /// W2b-5 (SCM-177): the place pickers take from (small quantities at hand), refilled from bulk.
  PICK_FACE
  /// W2b-5 (SCM-177): bulk storage (whole rolls, bundles of hides), which refills the pick faces.
  BULK
}

/// Why a location is blocked (SCM-181; the design's "count, damage, clean-up").
enum LocationBlockReason {
  /// A count runs there.
  COUNT
  DAMAGE
  CLEAN_UP
  /// Said in words (Location.blockNote).
  OTHER
}

/// Goods received from a supplier at a site (SCM-113), usually against a purchase order, with the supplier's DDT. OPEN
/// while its lines, lots and hides are written; POSTED when its moves are in the ledger; REVERSED (by reversing moves)
/// when it was wrong; CANCELLED when it never happened.
model GoodsReceipt {
  id                String             @id @db.Uuid
  tenantId          String             @default(dbgenerated("(NULLIF(current_setting('factory.tenant_id'::text, true), ''::text))::uuid")) @db.Uuid
  companyId         String             @db.Uuid
  siteId            String             @db.Uuid
  /// The number from the company's GOODS_RECEIPT series, unique in the company.
  number            String
  /// The supplier: the purchase order's party when one is named.
  supplierId        String             @db.Uuid
  /// The purchase order it receives against, delivered to this site; null for goods without an order.
  purchaseOrderId   String?            @db.Uuid
  /// W2b-5 (schema wave 36/44, B-W2b-277; SCM-122): STANDARD, or UNPLANNED: goods nobody ordered, received without a purchase
  /// order into a holding place and handed to a buyer; fixed once made. An UNPLANNED receipt is POSTED only once a purchase
  /// order names it: nothing of it is in stock, so nothing is used, until then.
  kind              GoodsReceiptKind   @default(STANDARD)
  /// W2b-5: UNPLANNED exactly: the place its goods wait in (a location of the receipt's site, not archived when named).
  holdingLocationId String?            @db.Uuid
  /// W2b-5: the buyer's task (a Task of this receipt that asks for the purchase order or a return), named once by the office
  /// while the receipt is OPEN; UNPLANNED only. Task has no tenant-safe key, so no reference: the trigger checks it.
  buyerTaskId       String?            @db.Uuid
  /// W2b (wave 22/22, B-W2b-158; SCM-106, B-W2b-182): the supplier's ship notice it was prefilled from: of the receipt's
  /// site, supplier and purchase order, SENT (or RECEIVED by an earlier receipt); set while the receipt is OPEN. It posts
  /// nothing by itself: the receipt's lines, lots and hides are what the dock counted and measured.
  shipNoticeId      String?            @db.Uuid
  /// The supplier's transport document (DDT, DPR 472/1996) the goods came with. W2b: still corrected once the receipt
  /// is POSTED (a number typed wrong at the dock), with the correction below.
  supplierDdtNumber String?
  supplierDdtDate   DateTime?          @db.Date
  /// W2b (B-W2a-31): the latest correction of the supplier's DDT number or date on a POSTED receipt: when, by whom and
  /// why (all three or none; the command's audit row keeps every one). None while OPEN.
  supplierDdtCorrectedAt      DateTime? @db.Timestamptz(3)
  supplierDdtCorrectedById    String?   @db.Uuid
  supplierDdtCorrectionReason String?
  receivedAt        DateTime           @db.Timestamptz(3)
  status            GoodsReceiptStatus @default(OPEN)
  note              String?
  /// Set exactly when POSTED or REVERSED.
  postedAt          DateTime?          @db.Timestamptz(3)
  postedById        String?            @db.Uuid
  /// Set exactly when REVERSED, with the reason.
  reversedAt        DateTime?          @db.Timestamptz(3)
  reversedById      String?            @db.Uuid
  reversalReason    String?
  /// Set exactly when CANCELLED.
  cancelledAt       DateTime?          @db.Timestamptz(3)
  version           Int                @default(1)
  createdAt         DateTime           @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt         DateTime           @default(now()) @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  createdById       String?            @db.Uuid

  site          Site               @relation(fields: [tenantId, companyId, siteId], references: [tenantId, companyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  supplier      Party              @relation(fields: [tenantId, supplierId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  purchaseOrder PurchaseOrder?     @relation(fields: [tenantId, siteId, purchaseOrderId], references: [tenantId, siteId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  // W2b (wave 22/22): its ship notice. Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default for an optional relation: that would also
  // clear tenantId, siteId and supplierId.
  shipNotice    ShipNotice?        @relation(fields: [tenantId, siteId, supplierId, shipNoticeId], references: [tenantId, siteId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  // W2b-5 (wave 36/44): the holding place of goods without a PO. Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default: that would also clear
  // tenantId and siteId.
  holdingLocation Location?        @relation("GoodsReceiptHolding", fields: [tenantId, siteId, holdingLocationId], references: [tenantId, siteId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  lines         GoodsReceiptLine[]
  // W2a claims.prisma: what was wrong with the delivery, and the claims about its goods.
  discrepancies  ReceiptDiscrepancy[]
  supplierClaims SupplierClaim[]

  @@unique([tenantId, companyId, number])
  // The target of the lines' reference: on the receipt's own site.
  @@unique([tenantId, siteId, id])
  // W2b (wave 22/22): the receipts of a ship notice.
  @@index([tenantId, shipNoticeId])
}

/// W2b-5 (SCM-122): what kind of delivery a receipt is.
enum GoodsReceiptKind {
  /// Goods received as W1 receives them: against a purchase order (or opening stock and the like without one).
  STANDARD
  /// Goods nobody ordered: held in a holding place for a buyer until a purchase order names them (or they go back).
  UNPLANNED
  /// W2b-5 (schema wave 39/44, B-W2b-281; SAL-306): goods a customer sends for its orders (the brand's own leather, trims):
  /// from a CUSTOMER or BRAND party, with no purchase order or ship notice, of materials tracked by LOT or HIDE; its lots are
  /// owned by the sender (Lot.ownerPartyId), never valued, never matched to a supplier invoice.
  CUSTOMER_SUPPLIED
}

/// OPEN → POSTED → REVERSED; OPEN → CANCELLED.
enum GoodsReceiptStatus {
  OPEN
  POSTED
  REVERSED
  CANCELLED
}

/// One material of a goods receipt: how much came, in which unit, against which purchase order line. Its lots (and
/// their hides) say how it came; its RECEIPT moves put it into the ledger. Changes only while the receipt is OPEN.
model GoodsReceiptLine {
  id                  String   @id @db.Uuid
  tenantId            String   @default(dbgenerated("(NULLIF(current_setting('factory.tenant_id'::text, true), ''::text))::uuid")) @db.Uuid
  siteId              String   @db.Uuid
  receiptId           String   @db.Uuid
  /// The line's place on the receipt: 10, 20, 30 …
  seq                 Int
  /// The purchase order line it receives against: a line of the receipt's purchase order, of the same item and colour.
  purchaseOrderLineId String?  @db.Uuid
  itemId              String   @db.Uuid
  itemColourId        String?  @db.Uuid
  /// Above 0, as counted or measured at the dock, in `uom`.
  quantity            Decimal  @db.Decimal(18, 4)
  uom                 Uom
  /// The same quantity in the item's base unit: what the line's RECEIPT moves add up to once the receipt is POSTED.
  baseQuantity        Decimal  @db.Decimal(18, 4)
  /// Leather: how many hides came (each a Hide of the line's lots).
  hideCount           Int?
  /// W2a (SCM-123): when the goods came counted in a unit whose size varies by delivery (rolls of different lengths, a
  /// box, the supplier's DDT unit): how many came in it (above 0), which unit, and how many of the item's base units one
  /// of it held at this receipt (above 0). Then baseQuantity = receivedQuantity × receivedFactor, rounded to 4 decimals
  /// (the …_supply_w2a_guards trigger); all three or none. quantity and uom stay the line's figure against the order.
  receivedQuantity    Decimal? @db.Decimal(18, 4)
  receivedUom         Uom?
  receivedFactor      Decimal? @db.Decimal(18, 8)
  note                String?
  version             Int      @default(1)
  createdAt           DateTime @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt           DateTime @default(now()) @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  createdById         String?  @db.Uuid

  receipt           GoodsReceipt       @relation(fields: [tenantId, siteId, receiptId], references: [tenantId, siteId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  purchaseOrderLine PurchaseOrderLine? @relation(fields: [tenantId, siteId, purchaseOrderLineId], references: [tenantId, siteId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  item              Item               @relation(fields: [tenantId, itemId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  itemColour        ItemColour?        @relation(fields: [tenantId, itemId, itemColourId], references: [tenantId, itemId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  lots              Lot[]
  moves             StockMove[]
  // W2a payables.prisma (wave 7/7): the supplier invoice lines matched against it (three-way match).
  supplierInvoiceMatches SupplierInvoiceMatch[]
  // W2a claims.prisma: the discrepancies and claim lines about it.
  discrepancies     ReceiptDiscrepancy[]
  claimLines        SupplierClaimLine[]

  @@unique([tenantId, receiptId, seq])
  // The target of the lots' and moves' references: on the line's own site.
  @@unique([tenantId, siteId, id])
}

/// A lot of one material in one colour at a site (SCM-116, SCM-232): a tannery dye batch, a fabric roll batch, a
/// protector batch, with our number and the supplier's. Its quality status is the hold of all its stock (and of its
/// hides): QUARANTINE until released (SCM-117), with its Cr VI result (QHS-029). Never deleted: a bad lot is REJECTED.
model Lot {
  id                 String           @id @db.Uuid
  tenantId           String           @default(dbgenerated("(NULLIF(current_setting('factory.tenant_id'::text, true), ''::text))::uuid")) @db.Uuid
  companyId          String           @db.Uuid
  siteId             String           @db.Uuid
  /// An item tracked by LOT or HIDE.
  itemId             String           @db.Uuid
  /// The colour the lot is (a dye batch is one colour).
  itemColourId       String?          @db.Uuid
  /// Our lot number (the LOT series), unique in the tenant; printed on its labels.
  code               String
  supplierId         String?          @db.Uuid
  /// The supplier's batch number.
  supplierLotRef     String?
  /// W2b-5 (schema wave 39/44, B-W2b-281; SAL-306, B-W2b-228): customer-owned stock: the customer or brand whose material
  /// it is (sent to us for its orders: a CUSTOMER_SUPPLIED receipt of that party, or opening stock); null: ours. Set when the
  /// lot is made, never changed. Never valued, never bought, never issued or reserved for another party's order (the
  /// …_sales_orders_depth_w2b_guards triggers, for every login).
  ownerPartyId       String?          @db.Uuid
  /// The tannery's dye batch (one shade).
  dyeBatch           String?
  shade              String?
  /// The receipt line it came with; null for opening stock (B-W1-35).
  receiptLineId      String?          @db.Uuid
  receivedAt         DateTime?        @db.Timestamptz(3)
  qualityStatus      LotQualityStatus @default(QUARANTINE)
  /// Why it was released, rejected or blocked.
  qualityNote        String?
  /// Set from the first decision on (any status but QUARANTINE).
  qualityDecidedAt   DateTime?        @db.Timestamptz(3)
  qualityDecidedById String?          @db.Uuid
  /// Copied from the item at receipt and never changed: the lot needs Cr VI evidence before release.
  requiresCrViTest   Boolean          @default(false)
  /// The limit it must stay below, mg/kg (the item's: the legal 3, or a brand's lower one); set exactly when tested.
  crViLimitMgKg      Decimal?         @db.Decimal(8, 3)
  /// NOT_REQUIRED for a lot without the test; PENDING → PASS | FAIL (PASS → FAIL on later evidence).
  crViStatus         CrViStatus       @default(NOT_REQUIRED)
  /// The measured Cr VI content, mg/kg: at or above the limit is a FAIL.
  crViMgKg           Decimal?         @db.Decimal(8, 3)
  /// What the result rests on (the evidence rule is a setting, Q14); the report itself is a file of the lot.
  crViEvidence       CrViEvidence?
  crViTestedAt       DateTime?        @db.Date
  /// W2b-5 (schema wave 36/44, B-W2b-277; SCM-236): where the lot is in its life, beside its quality status (W1's, which
  /// holds the stock and which every W1 path reads): QUARANTINE → RELEASED → IN_USE (the first issue) → DEPLETED (the last
  /// unit out); BLOCKED; RETURNED (back to its supplier). It fits the quality status (QUARANTINE exactly while QUARANTINE;
  /// RELEASED and IN_USE only RELEASED; BLOCKED only BLOCKED or REJECTED), and the database moves it when a quality decision
  /// leaves it unfitting (…_warehouse_depth_w2b_guards: to QUARANTINE, RELEASED or BLOCKED; a REJECTED lot BLOCKED until its
  /// stock left). The inventory module moves it by the events (B-W2b-313).
  lifecycle          LotLifecycle     @default(QUARANTINE)
  /// W2b-5 (SCM-237; B-W2b-80, -98): the lot it was split from (a shade group of it): of the same site, item and colour, a
  /// lot that is no child itself; set when it is made, never changed.
  parentLotId        String?          @db.Uuid
  /// W2b-5 (SCM-185): what was measured or declared of this lot, typed per material kind (decimals as strings): LEATHER {
  /// "thicknessMinMm", "thicknessMaxMm" (above 0, at most 20, min ≤ max), "finish", "tannage" (CHROME, VEGETABLE,
  /// CHROME_FREE, COMBINATION), "gradeMix" { "<grade code>": "<percent>" (above 0, adding up to at most 100) }, "origin" };
  /// TEXTILE, LINING, MEMBRANE, PADDING { "widthCm", "weightGsm", "origin" }; any other kind { "origin" }; texts 1 to 100
  /// characters. {}: nothing recorded.
  attributes         Json             @default("{}")
  /// W2b-5 (schema wave 40/44, B-W2b-285; SCM-186): the variant of the item the lot is (buying-depth.prisma ItemVariant, by
  /// its code; of the lot's colour when the variant has one, ACTIVE when named); set when the lot is made (or once on an
  /// older lot), never changed. A lot received on a purchase order line of a variant is of that variant.
  variantCode        String?
  version            Int              @default(1)
  createdAt          DateTime         @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt          DateTime         @default(now()) @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  createdById        String?          @db.Uuid

  site        Site              @relation(fields: [tenantId, companyId, siteId], references: [tenantId, companyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  item        Item              @relation(fields: [tenantId, itemId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  // W2b-5 (wave 40/44): its variant (Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default: that would also clear tenantId and itemId).
  variant     ItemVariant?      @relation(fields: [tenantId, itemId, variantCode], references: [tenantId, itemId, code], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  itemColour  ItemColour?       @relation(fields: [tenantId, itemId, itemColourId], references: [tenantId, itemId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  supplier    Party?            @relation(fields: [tenantId, supplierId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  receiptLine GoodsReceiptLine? @relation(fields: [tenantId, siteId, receiptLineId], references: [tenantId, siteId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  // W2b-5 (wave 39/44): the customer who owns it. Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default: that would also clear tenantId.
  owner       Party?            @relation("LotOwner", fields: [tenantId, ownerPartyId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  hides       Hide[]
  moves       StockMove[]
  valuations  StockValuation[]
  // W2a reservations.prisma, stockcount.prisma: its reservations, the counts of it and the count lines of it.
  reservations    Reservation[]
  stockCounts     StockCount[]
  stockCountLines StockCountLine[]
  // quality.prisma: its lab results (the Cr VI result's history) and supplier documents (B-W1-34).
  labResults  LabResult[]
  documents   LotDocument[]
  // W2b inspection-plans.prisma (wave 10/16): its incoming inspections.
  incomingInspections IncomingInspection[]
  // W2b leather.prisma (wave 12/16): its own shade groups, its fabric rolls, the garments that hold it (a protector lot).
  shadeGroups         ShadeGroup[]
  fabricRolls         FabricRoll[]
  garmentProtectors   GarmentProtectorLot[]
  // W2b-2 cutting.prisma (wave 13/16): the recut tickets cut from it (the same shade lot).
  recutTickets        CutTicket[]
  // W2a ncr.prisma: the nonconformances about it.
  nonconformances Nonconformance[]
  // W2b-4 samples.prisma (wave 29/33): the swatches of it sent to brands.
  sampleSwatches  SampleSwatch[]
  // W2a claims.prisma, subcontract.prisma: the claim lines and kit lines that name it.
  claimLines  SupplierClaimLine[]
  kitLines    SubcontractKitLine[]
  // W2b-5 (wave 36/44): the lot it was split from and its child lots (Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default: that would also
  // clear tenantId, siteId and itemId); warehouse-depth.prisma: the transfer lines that send it or that it arrived as, the
  // tasks that handle it, the substitutions that use it.
  parentLot         Lot?                   @relation("LotSplit", fields: [tenantId, siteId, itemId, parentLotId], references: [tenantId, siteId, itemId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  childLots         Lot[]                  @relation("LotSplit")
  transferLines     TransferLine[]         @relation("TransferLineLot")
  transferLinesIn   TransferLine[]         @relation("TransferLineToLot")
  warehouseTasks    WarehouseTask[]
  substitutions     MaterialSubstitution[]

  @@unique([tenantId, code])
  // The target of the hides', moves' and valuations' references: a lot of the same site and item.
  @@unique([tenantId, siteId, itemId, id])
  // W2b-5: the child lots of a lot.
  @@index([tenantId, parentLotId])
}

/// W2b-5 (SCM-236): where a lot is in its life (Lot.lifecycle), beside its quality status.
enum LotLifecycle {
  /// Waiting for its release (quality QUARANTINE).
  QUARANTINE
  /// Released, nothing issued yet.
  RELEASED
  /// Released, issued from.
  IN_USE
  /// Nothing of it left.
  DEPLETED
  /// Held (quality BLOCKED, or REJECTED until its stock left).
  BLOCKED
  /// Sent back to its supplier.
  RETURNED
}

/// QUARANTINE → RELEASED | REJECTED | BLOCKED; RELEASED → BLOCKED; BLOCKED → RELEASED | REJECTED. Only RELEASED is usable.
enum LotQualityStatus {
  QUARANTINE
  RELEASED
  /// Final: returned to the supplier or scrapped.
  REJECTED
  /// Held after a release (a later finding, a recall).
  BLOCKED
}

enum CrViStatus {
  NOT_REQUIRED
  PENDING
  PASS
  FAIL
}

/// What a Cr VI result rests on (setting Q14).
enum CrViEvidence {
  /// A lab report on this lot.
  LOT_REPORT
  /// The supplier's report covering the article and the period.
  SUPPLIER_REPORT
}

/// One hide (or skin) of a lot, received one by one (SCM-233, SCM-247): its tag, its own measured area, grade, shade,
/// thickness and defects. Its stock is the ledger's (the moves that name it); its state is what cutting left of it
/// (SCM-253): FULL, PARTLY_CUT, REMNANT, CONSUMED, SCRAPPED.
model Hide {
  id           String    @id @db.Uuid
  tenantId     String    @default(dbgenerated("(NULLIF(current_setting('factory.tenant_id'::text, true), ''::text))::uuid")) @db.Uuid
  siteId       String    @db.Uuid
  lotId        String    @db.Uuid
  /// The lot's item (tracked by HIDE).
  itemId       String    @db.Uuid
  /// Our tag (barcode), unique in the tenant; printed on the hide tag (B-W1-33) and scanned at cutting.
  code         String
  /// The tannery's own number on the hide, when it has one.
  supplierCode String?
  /// The area as measured at receipt, above 0, in an area unit (M2, DM2, FT2). Never changed: a correction is an
  /// adjustment move.
  area         Decimal   @db.Decimal(18, 4)
  areaUom      Uom
  /// The same area in the item's base unit: what its receipt move adds.
  baseArea     Decimal   @db.Decimal(18, 4)
  /// W1's text, kept so labels and history stay valid. With gradeId set it is that grade's code.
  grade        String?
  /// W1's text, kept likewise. With shadeGroupId set it is that group's label.
  shade        String?
  /// W2b (wave 12/16, SCM-250): the grade as a record, a grade of the tenant's list; null: a hide graded in text only.
  gradeId      String?   @db.Uuid
  /// W2b (wave 12/16, QHS-028): the shade group, of the hide's article, colour and lot (the …_leather_stock_w2b_guards
  /// trigger); null: not sorted against a swatch.
  shadeGroupId String?   @db.Uuid
  thicknessMm  Decimal?  @db.Decimal(6, 2)
  /// Defects seen (holes, scars, brand marks) and where; its photos are its files.
  defects      String?
  state        HideState @default(FULL)
  /// W2b (B-W2a-11, -44): the state it had before it became SCRAPPED or RETURNED, written by the database itself when it
  /// moves there (the …_followups_stock_w2b_guards trigger) and cleared when it comes back to it; null otherwise (and on
  /// a hide scrapped before W2b: it stays SCRAPPED).
  previousState HideState?
  /// Set exactly while the hide is CONSUMED: the cut log entry after which nothing of it was left (the Hide done's
  /// entry, or the last cut when Hide done used nothing more). Reversing that entry, and only that one, opens the hide
  /// again (CONSUMED → PARTLY_CUT, this cleared): a wrong closing cut is corrected (B-W1-40's gap).
  closingCutLogId String? @db.Uuid
  version      Int       @default(1)
  createdAt    DateTime  @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt    DateTime  @default(now()) @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  createdById  String?   @db.Uuid

  lot   Lot         @relation(fields: [tenantId, siteId, itemId, lotId], references: [tenantId, siteId, itemId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  moves StockMove[]
  // W2a reservations.prisma, stockcount.prisma: its reservations and the count lines of it.
  reservations    Reservation[]
  stockCountLines StockCountLine[]
  // production.prisma: the cut log entries of the hide.
  cutLogs CutLog[] @relation("HideCutLogs")
  // W2b inspection-plans.prisma (wave 10/16): its rows in incoming inspections.
  incomingResults IncomingHideResult[]
  // W2b leather.prisma (wave 12/16): its grade and shade group (Restrict, as below), its marks, measures and remnants.
  leatherGrade LeatherGrade? @relation(fields: [tenantId, gradeId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  shadeGroup   ShadeGroup?   @relation(fields: [tenantId, shadeGroupId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  marks        HideMark[]
  measures     HideMeasure[]
  remnants     Remnant[]
  // Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default for an optional relation: that would also clear tenantId and siteId.
  closingCutLog CutLog? @relation("HideClosingCutLog", fields: [tenantId, siteId, closingCutLogId], references: [tenantId, siteId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  // W2a claims.prisma, subcontract.prisma: the claim lines and kit lines that name it.
  claimLines    SupplierClaimLine[]
  kitLines      SubcontractKitLine[]
  // W2b-5 warehouse-depth.prisma (wave 36/44): the transfer lines that send it or that it arrived as, the tasks that handle it.
  transferLines   TransferLine[]  @relation("TransferLineHide")
  transferLinesIn TransferLine[]  @relation("TransferLineToHide")
  warehouseTasks  WarehouseTask[]

  @@unique([tenantId, code])
  // The target of the moves' reference: a hide of the move's own site and lot.
  @@unique([tenantId, siteId, lotId, id])
  // W2b: find hides by grade and shade group (SCM-257).
  @@index([tenantId, gradeId])
  @@index([tenantId, shadeGroupId])
}

/// FULL → PARTLY_CUT | REMNANT | CONSUMED | SCRAPPED | RETURNED; between PARTLY_CUT and REMNANT freely; CONSUMED is
/// final but for one move: CONSUMED → PARTLY_CUT when its closing cut log entry is reversed. W2b: SCRAPPED and RETURNED
/// are final but for one move: back to the state it had (previousState) once the SCRAP (SUPPLIER_RETURN) move that took
/// it out is reversed.
enum HideState {
  FULL
  PARTLY_CUT
  /// What is left after cutting, back in stock as an offcut.
  REMNANT
  CONSUMED
  SCRAPPED
  /// W2b (B-W2a-44): sent back to the tannery (a SUPPLIER_RETURN move took it out).
  RETURNED
}

/// One movement of stock (SCM-189): the append-only ledger of the site's stock. Never changed or removed (the
/// …_supply_guards triggers, for every login); a mistake is fixed with a reversal or an adjustment.
/// @append-only
model StockMove {
  id             String          @id @db.Uuid
  tenantId       String          @default(dbgenerated("(NULLIF(current_setting('factory.tenant_id'::text, true), ''::text))::uuid")) @db.Uuid
  /// The company that owns the stock: the site's.
  companyId      String          @db.Uuid
  siteId         String          @db.Uuid
  reason         StockMoveReason
  itemId         String          @db.Uuid
  itemColourId   String?         @db.Uuid
  /// Required for an item tracked by LOT or HIDE; a lot of the same item and colour.
  lotId          String?         @db.Uuid
  /// Required for an item tracked by HIDE; a hide of the lot.
  hideId         String?         @db.Uuid
  /// The location it leaves; null when it comes from outside the site's stock (a supplier, a work order, opening stock).
  fromLocationId String?         @db.Uuid
  /// The location it enters; null when it leaves the site's stock (to a work order, to scrap).
  toLocationId   String?         @db.Uuid
  /// Above 0, as entered, in `uom`.
  quantity       Decimal         @db.Decimal(18, 4)
  uom            Uom
  /// Above 0, in the item's base unit: what the balances add up.
  baseQuantity   Decimal         @db.Decimal(18, 4)
  /// RECEIPT: the goods receipt line it posts.
  receiptLineId  String?         @db.Uuid
  /// ISSUE, RETURN, PRODUCTION_RECEIPT: the work order (the production schema, W1-23, brings its table; a plain id
  /// until then).
  workOrderId    String?         @db.Uuid
  /// A human reference: the work order number, the count sheet, the supplier's DDT.
  reference      String?
  /// Why; required for an ADJUSTMENT, a COUNT difference and a SCRAP (SCM-192), unless the reason code says it (W2b).
  note           String?
  /// W2b (B-W2a-11, -18): the code of the reason list the move was made for, as text (records keep the code, never a
  /// reference: reasons.prisma): WRITE_OFF for a write-off's SCRAP, ADJUSTMENT for an adjustment or a count, the scrap
  /// list (ScrapReason) for production scrap, CLAIM for goods back to a supplier, RETURN for goods back from a customer.
  /// Not blank and without spaces when set; the API checks it against the tenant's list.
  reasonCode     String?
  /// W2b (B-W2a-43): CUSTOMER_RETURN, exactly: the return line whose goods it puts into stock (a line of an RMA of the
  /// move's company and site), and that line's customer (the reference's key: ReturnLine is keyed by its party).
  returnPartyId  String?         @db.Uuid
  returnLineId   String?         @db.Uuid
  /// W2b (B-W2a-48): SHIPMENT, exactly: the shipment line (of the move's site and company) whose garments leave
  /// finished-goods stock.
  shipmentLineId String?         @db.Uuid
  /// W2b-5 (schema wave 36/44, B-W2b-277; SCM-219, SCM-220): the transfer line it carries: TRANSFER_OUT and TRANSFER_IN
  /// exactly; also the ship's TRANSFER onto the transfer's transit location and an ADJUSTMENT that writes a difference off
  /// it. A move into or out of a TRANSIT location always names one (the …_warehouse_depth_w2b_guards trigger).
  transferLineId String?         @db.Uuid
  /// W2b-5 (SCM-196): the day it counts on in the books (Europe/Rome) when it is not the day it happened: not after the day
  /// it was entered, not further back than the company's back-dating limit (InventorySettings), never inside a closed period
  /// (the period lock reads it); a floor session posts today's. null: the day it happened (occurredAt).
  postingDate    DateTime?       @db.Date
  /// The move this one reverses: the same move with its locations swapped. At most one reversal per move.
  reversalOfId   String?         @db.Uuid
  /// Unique in the tenant: the command's idempotency key, so a retried scan or request posts once.
  idempotencyKey String
  /// When it happened: the device's time for a floor scan (createdAt is the server's).
  occurredAt     DateTime        @db.Timestamptz(3)
  /// The floor device it was posted from.
  deviceId       String?         @db.Uuid
  createdAt      DateTime        @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  /// The office user or floor worker who posted it.
  createdById    String?         @db.Uuid

  site         Site              @relation(fields: [tenantId, companyId, siteId], references: [tenantId, companyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  item         Item              @relation(fields: [tenantId, itemId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  // Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default for an optional relation: that would also clear tenantId and siteId.
  itemColour   ItemColour?       @relation(fields: [tenantId, itemId, itemColourId], references: [tenantId, itemId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  lot          Lot?              @relation(fields: [tenantId, siteId, itemId, lotId], references: [tenantId, siteId, itemId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  hide         Hide?             @relation(fields: [tenantId, siteId, lotId, hideId], references: [tenantId, siteId, lotId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  fromLocation Location?         @relation("StockMoveFrom", fields: [tenantId, siteId, fromLocationId], references: [tenantId, siteId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  toLocation   Location?         @relation("StockMoveTo", fields: [tenantId, siteId, toLocationId], references: [tenantId, siteId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  receiptLine  GoodsReceiptLine? @relation(fields: [tenantId, siteId, receiptLineId], references: [tenantId, siteId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  reversalOf   StockMove?        @relation("StockMoveReversal", fields: [tenantId, siteId, reversalOfId], references: [tenantId, siteId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  reversals    StockMove[]       @relation("StockMoveReversal")
  // W2a stockcount.prisma: the count line whose difference it posts (a COUNT move).
  stockCountLines StockCountLine[]
  // W2a ncr.prisma: the NCR decision it carried out (a scrap, a move to quarantine).
  ncrDispositionLines NcrDispositionLine[]
  device       Device?           @relation(fields: [tenantId, siteId, deviceId], references: [tenantId, siteId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  valuations   StockValuation[]
  // W2a cost-ledger.prisma (wave 7/7): the work-order cost entries it posted (an issue, a return, a scrap).
  /// @not-money the relation to the cost ledger (the rows carry the grain)
  costEntries  WorkOrderCostEntry[]
  // W2a claims.prisma, subcontract.prisma: the claim line it returned, the kit line it sent.
  claimLines   SupplierClaimLine[]
  kitLines     SubcontractKitLine[]
  // W2b leather.prisma (wave 12/16): the remnants it put into stock.
  remnants     Remnant[]
  // W2b-4 cutting.prisma (wave 24/33): the downgrade whose garments it put into second-quality stock.
  garmentDowngrades GarmentDowngrade[]
  // W2b (B-W2b-01): the return line a CUSTOMER_RETURN puts into stock and the shipment line a SHIPMENT takes out
  // (Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default for an optional relation: that would also clear tenantId and siteId).
  returnLine   ReturnLine?       @relation(fields: [tenantId, returnPartyId, returnLineId], references: [tenantId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  shipmentLine ShipmentLine?     @relation(fields: [tenantId, siteId, shipmentLineId], references: [tenantId, siteId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  // W2b-5 warehouse-depth.prisma (wave 36/44): the transfer line it carries (Restrict, as above).
  transferLine TransferLine?     @relation(fields: [tenantId, transferLineId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  @@unique([tenantId, idempotencyKey])
  // The target of the reversals' and valuations' references: on the move's own site.
  @@unique([tenantId, siteId, id])
  // The balances: the moves of one stock key.
  @@index([tenantId, siteId, itemId, lotId, hideId])
  // W2b: the moves of a return line and of a shipment line.
  @@index([tenantId, returnLineId])
  @@index([tenantId, shipmentLineId])
  // W2b-5: the moves of a transfer line.
  @@index([tenantId, transferLineId])
}

/// Why stock moved. Into the site's stock: OPENING, RECEIPT, RETURN, REMNANT, PRODUCTION_RECEIPT, CUSTOMER_RETURN, TRANSFER_IN;
/// out of it: ISSUE, SCRAP, SUPPLIER_RETURN, SHIPMENT, TRANSFER_OUT; inside it: TRANSFER; either way: ADJUSTMENT, COUNT.
enum StockMoveReason {
  /// Stock the site held before the factory app (B-W1-35).
  OPENING
  /// Goods from a supplier, posting a goods receipt line.
  RECEIPT
  /// To a work order: only RELEASED stock.
  ISSUE
  /// Back from a work order (a remnant, unused material).
  RETURN
  TRANSFER
  /// A correction with its reason (SCM-192).
  ADJUSTMENT
  /// A count difference.
  COUNT
  SCRAP
  /// W2a (GAP-003, MES-011): finished garments of a work order (StockMove.workOrderId) into finished-goods stock, as the
  /// FINISHED item of their SKU, partial or whole; never more than the work order's cell makes (the …_production_w2a_guards
  /// trigger).
  PRODUCTION_RECEIPT
  /// W2b (B-W2a-43): goods back from a customer put into stock by the return's decision (restock, second quality,
  /// quarantine), naming the return line (StockMove.returnLineId).
  CUSTOMER_RETURN
  /// W2b (B-W2a-44): goods sent back to their supplier (a supplier claim's return; the claim line names the move).
  SUPPLIER_RETURN
  /// W2b (B-W2a-48): garments leaving finished-goods stock with a shipment, naming the shipment line
  /// (StockMove.shipmentLineId).
  SHIPMENT
  /// W2b (wave 12/16, SCM-254): an offcut back from a work order as tagged stock (a Remnant names the move): RETURN's twin,
  /// by every rule of the database (it enters one location, names its work order, comes off what the work order holds).
  REMNANT
  /// W2b-5 (schema wave 36/44, SCM-219, SCM-220): goods received at another site of the tenant leave this site's stock: out
  /// of the transfer's transit location, naming the transfer line (StockMove.transferLineId); posted with its TRANSFER_IN.
  TRANSFER_OUT
  /// W2b-5: goods sent from another site enter this site's stock with the receipt of a transfer, naming the transfer line,
  /// as the lot (and hide) the receipt made here.
  TRANSFER_IN
}

/// The value of one move that changes the site's stock value (A1 §2.6: a cost, office only): its signed base quantity
/// (+ into the site's stock, − out of it), the unit cost it is valued at and the amount. Never changed or removed; a
/// wrong value is corrected by the move's reversal and a new move, each valued.
/// @append-only
model StockValuation {
  id             String               @id @db.Uuid
  tenantId       String               @default(dbgenerated("(NULLIF(current_setting('factory.tenant_id'::text, true), ''::text))::uuid")) @db.Uuid
  /// The move's company and site.
  companyId      String               @db.Uuid
  siteId         String               @db.Uuid
  moveId         String               @db.Uuid
  /// The move's item and lot.
  itemId         String               @db.Uuid
  lotId          String?              @db.Uuid
  /// The move's base quantity, signed: + when it entered the site's stock, − when it left it.
  quantity       Decimal              @db.Decimal(18, 4)
  /// Per base unit, in `currency`.
  /// @grain cost
  unitCost       Decimal              @db.Decimal(18, 6)
  /// quantity × unit cost, rounded to minor units, signed like the quantity.
  /// @grain cost
  valueAmount    Int
  currency       String               @default("EUR")
  method         StockValuationMethod
  /// Unique in the tenant: one valuation per move (`move:<moveId>`), so a retried handler values it once.
  idempotencyKey String
  note           String?
  createdAt      DateTime             @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  createdById    String?              @db.Uuid

  site Site      @relation(fields: [tenantId, companyId, siteId], references: [tenantId, companyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  move StockMove @relation(fields: [tenantId, siteId, moveId], references: [tenantId, siteId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  item Item      @relation(fields: [tenantId, itemId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  lot  Lot?      @relation(fields: [tenantId, siteId, itemId, lotId], references: [tenantId, siteId, itemId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  @@unique([tenantId, idempotencyKey])
}

enum StockValuationMethod {
  /// A receipt, at its purchase order line's price.
  PURCHASE_PRICE
  /// Stock leaving, at the cost its lot came in with.
  LOT_COST
  /// At the item's standard cost (opening stock, untracked items).
  STANDARD_COST
  /// Typed by the office with a reason (an adjustment).
  MANUAL
}
